extra['phase2-batch2-low-healthrx-vs-agelessrx-20260723'].append({'h2':'Decision record for this pair','paragraphs':["The final comparison record should state why each provider received its score, which captured sentence supports every populated cell, and which omissions remained unknown. For HealthRX, the record should preserve the separate approval and shipping clocks, payment tools, and no-long-term-commitment statement. For AgelessRx, it should preserve the monthly and multi-month formats, no-membership-fee language, and post-processing delivery window. A future editor should be able to reproduce the table without reading this narrative first.","Before any release, re-open both provider pages, compare the live wording with the archived quotes, rerun the score, and inspect the page for active outbound routes. If the evidence changes, revise the row and version the receipt. If the operator does not approve go-live, the correct state remains held even when every editorial field passes. The release receipt must bind the refreshed sources, score, and frozen rendered page."]})
extra['phase2-batch2-low-wellorithm-vs-enhance-md-20260723'].append({'h2':'Decision record for this pair','paragraphs':["The audit record for Wellorithm should foreground the introductory-to-recurring transition, route language, financing, refrigeration statement, consultation window, and delivery window. The Enhance.MD record should foreground its flat captured monthly figures, approval language, provider and nutrition support, HSA/FSA statement, no-insurance statement, and delivery range. Keeping those records separate prevents a later editor from collapsing distinct offers into a generic affordability article.","Release review should recapture the official pages, compare every quoted amount and timeline, rerun the score, and remeasure similarity against nearby commercial pages. If either source becomes ambiguous, the affected field returns to unknown. Editorial completion never activates a redirect, sends a lead, or authorizes a provider relationship. The reviewer should also compare the rendered article with every adjacent money page and commercial guide, record the maximum vocabulary overlap, confirm that the billing-period distinctions remain visible on mobile, and bind those checks to the revised packet. If consolidation removes a weaker angle, the sitemap and keyword ledger must remove it too rather than leave an orphan doorway. The final mobile check must show the introductory amount, later recurring amount, route, and unknown terms without forcing readers to infer them from a collapsed table cell."]})
extra['phase2-batch2-medium-verify-product-status-and-online-program-evidence-20260723'].append({'h2':'The stopping condition is part of verification','paragraphs':["Research should end with an explicit verdict: source-clear, held for a named gap, or excluded at a hard boundary. “More research needed” is not useful unless the missing artifact is identified—for example, recurring price, product formulation, pharmacy identity, service-area support, cancellation terms, or warning-letter resolution. A bounded ledger keeps the team from padding the roster or revisiting the same inaccessible claim without new evidence.","For this batch, the stopping condition produced thirteen comparison-ready programs across both accepted batches and six documented exclusions. That exhaustion claim is about the current curated evidence pool, not the entire telehealth market. New programs can enter only through a fresh research and compliance gate. Exhaustion must be versioned with the registry and source hashes so a later candidate, updated warning status, or newly accessible official page can reopen the boundary without rewriting history. Until that happens, the honest next action is maintenance and correction, not another thin top-list expansion."]})
